---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Contact Town Hall
eyebrow: Contact
lede: Phone numbers, hours, where to park, and how to reach a specific office.
breadcrumbs: []
---

{% include "partials/page-header.njk" %}

<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_20rem]">
    <div class="prose-gov">
      <h2>Town Hall</h2>
      <p>
        {{ site.address.line1 }}<br />
        {{ site.address.line2 }}<br />
        {{ site.address.city }}, {{ site.address.state }} {{ site.address.zip }}
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Main line:</strong> {{ site.phone }}<br />
        <strong>Fax:</strong> {{ site.fax }}<br />
        <strong>Email:</strong> {{ site.email }}<br />
        <strong>Hours:</strong> {{ site.hours }}
      </p>
      <p>
        Town Hall is closed on New Year's Day, Martin Luther King Jr. Day, Presidents'
        Day, Memorial Day, Juneteenth, Independence Day, Labor Day, Veterans Day,
        Thanksgiving and the day after, and Christmas Day.
      </p>

      <h2>Emergency and after-hours</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Emergencies:</strong> 911</li>
        <li><strong>Police non-emergency:</strong> (609) 555-0155</li>
        <li><strong>Public Works emergency (24 hours):</strong> (609) 555-0139</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Use the Public Works emergency line for water main breaks, sewer backups,
        downed trees blocking a road, and road hazards outside business hours.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting here and parking</h2>
      <p>
        Town Hall sits at the corner of Marsh Landing Road and Bay Street. Free public
        parking is in the lot behind the building, entered from Bay Street. Four
        accessible spaces are next to the rear entrance, which is the step-free way in.
        Route 3 stops at Marsh Landing and Bay.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>During the culvert closure through August 29,</strong> reach the lot from
        the Bay Street side; the Marsh Landing approach is closed to through traffic.
      </p>

      <h2>Emergency alerts</h2>
      <p>
        Osprey Point uses the Sedgemere County alert system for evacuations, boil-water
        notices, and severe weather. Registration is free and takes a couple of minutes.
        You choose text, voice, email, or all three. The town does not use the system for
        routine announcements.
      </p>

      <h2>Accessibility</h2>
      <p>
        Town Hall and Council Chambers are wheelchair accessible, and Chambers has an
        assistive listening system. Requests for interpretation, materials in an
        alternate format, or other accommodations should reach the Town Clerk at least
        five business days ahead at (609) 555-0111.
      </p>
      <p>
        To report a barrier to access or file an ADA grievance, contact the Town Manager's
        office at (609) 555-0110.
      </p>

      <h2>Media inquiries</h2>
      <p>
        Press contacts route through the Office of the Town Manager at (609) 555-0110.
        Department staff will refer media questions there.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="no-print space-y-6">
      <div class="rounded border border-navy-100 bg-navy-50 p-5">
        <h2 class="font-display text-base font-bold">Department lines</h2>
        <dl class="mt-3 space-y-2.5 text-sm">
          {% for dept in collections.departments %}
            <div>
              <dt>
                <a href="{{ dept.url }}" class="font-semibold text-bay-700 no-underline hover:underline"
                  >{{ dept.data.title }}</a
                >
              </dt>
              <dd class="text-navy-700">{{ dept.data.phone }}</dd>
            </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded border border-navy-100 p-5">
        <h2 class="font-display text-base font-bold">Looking for a person?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-navy-700">
          The
          <a href="/directory/" class="text-bay-700 underline underline-offset-2">staff directory</a>
          lists every office with a direct line. Elected officials are on the
          <a href="/government/council/" class="text-bay-700 underline underline-offset-2">Town Council</a>
          page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</div>
